Agent Software Factory Commercial Licence, version 1.0 (draft)

DRAFT: to be reviewed by a lawyer before the first public release (roadmap phase E). Until then this
text states the intended terms; the Licensor may replace it with the reviewed version.

1. Definitions
"Licensor" means the copyright holder named in the NOTICE file in this directory.
"Software" means the files in the directory that contains this LICENSE file (the "licensed/" directory
of the Agent Software Factory repository), in source or compiled form, and any modified version of them.
"Subscription" means a current, paid agreement with the Licensor that names the features and the term it
covers, evidenced by a licence key issued by the Licensor.
"Production Use" means any use of the Software other than Development Use.
"Development Use" means using the Software to develop, test, evaluate or demonstrate it, or to develop
and test changes to it, in a non-production environment.

2. What you may do
2.1 You may read, copy and modify the Software, and use it for Development Use, without a Subscription.
2.2 You may make Production Use of the features a valid Subscription covers, for its term, on the number
of installations it covers.
2.3 You may contribute changes to the Software back to the Licensor. Contributions are accepted under the
terms in CONTRIBUTING (Developer Certificate of Origin).

3. What you may not do
3.1 Make Production Use of the Software, or of any feature of it, without a valid Subscription covering
that feature.
3.2 Remove, disable, bypass or work around the licence key check, or any part of the Software that
enforces this licence, or make the Software accept a key the Licensor did not issue.
3.3 Provide the Software, or any feature of it, to third parties as a hosted or managed service.
3.4 Sell, sublicense or distribute the Software, modified or not, except copies for Development Use that
keep this LICENSE and the NOTICE file.
3.5 Remove or change any licence, copyright or other notice in the Software.

4. The rest of the repository
Everything outside the "licensed/" directory is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see the LICENSE file
at the repository root). This licence does not limit your rights under that licence to anything outside
"licensed/". Using the Apache-2.0 core alone never needs a Subscription.

5. Ending
Your rights under section 2.2 end when your Subscription ends. Your rights under this licence end
automatically if you break section 3; they come back if you stop and the breach is cured within 30 days of
notice from the Licensor, once only.

6. No warranty, limited liability
The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a
particular purpose and non-infringement, except as a Subscription agreement states otherwise. To the extent
the law allows, the Licensor is not liable for any damages arising from the Software or its use, except as a
Subscription agreement states otherwise.

7. Governing law
This licence is governed by the laws of England and Wales.
